# Cargo manifests

## Member crates inherit the workspace

```toml
[package]
name = "shellzip-<name>"
version.workspace = true
edition.workspace = true
license.workspace = true
publish.workspace = true
description = "One line, no trailing period"

[lints]
workspace = true   # unsafe_code = "forbid", clippy::all = warn
```

- Add new members to `[workspace] members` and, if they should build by default, `default-members`.
- `rust-version` and `edition` are set once at the workspace root; never override per crate.

## Dependencies

- Minimal and explicit: `default-features = false` plus the features used, e.g. `zip = { version = "2", default-features = false, features = ["deflate", "zstd", "time"] }`.
- Once two members share a dependency, move it to `[workspace.dependencies]` and reference it with `name.workspace = true`.
- Test-only crates belong in `[dev-dependencies]` (`tempfile`, `assert_cmd`, `predicates`, `proptest`, `insta`, `criterion`).
- Members reference each other by path: `shellzip-core = { path = "../shellzip-core" }`.
- Licenses: MIT / Apache-2.0 / BSD-compatible only; no GPL-only crates.
- Edit with `cargo add` / `cargo rm`. `Cargo.lock` is committed and never edited by hand.

## Features

- Optional formats and heavy deps are features: `rar = ["dep:unrar"]`, `sevenz = ["dep:zesven"]`, `sevenz-codecs = ["sevenz", "zesven/deflate", "zesven/bzip2", "zesven/ppmd", "zesven/zstd"]`. Features are additive and must not change behaviour of code paths that don't use them.
- Keep `default` small; document each feature in the crate-level `//!` docs.

## Binaries and profiles

- Name binaries explicitly: `[[bin]] name = "szip" path = "src/main.rs"`.
- Profiles live only in the root `Cargo.toml`:

```toml
[profile.release]
lto = true
codegen-units = 1
strip = true

[profile.minisize]      # SFX stub and other size-sensitive bins
inherits = "release"
opt-level = "z"
panic = "abort"
```
